"use strict";(self.webpackChunkchatgpt_shortcut=self.webpackChunkchatgpt_shortcut||[]).push([["13473"],{293139(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"id":14422,"title":"SAAs_entp","description":"# \u{1F3D7}\uFE0F guide building system ERP with Claude \u2014 Step by Step\\n\\n> You give one file to Cloud so that he can build a complete ERP system with you **in stages** \u2014 not all at once.\\n> The basic idea: Each stage is separate, Claude finishes it, **stops**, you review and experiment, and then you move on to the next one.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \u{1F4CC} How Used The file This\\n\\n1. Create a new empty folder for the system (e.g., ` erp -system` ) and open it in Cloud Code .\\n2. Copy the section **\u201C Golden Rules\u201D * below into a file named ` CLAUDE.md` inside the project \u2014 this makes Cloud adhere to the style in every session .\\n3. When you are ready for any stage, copy its ** ready Prompt ** only (not all stages) and send it to Cloud.\\n4. Claude finishes the stage \u2192 **stops** \u2192 You test and make sure it works \u2192 Then the next stage begins.\\n5. ** Don\'t let him skip stages** or build anything that is not within the scope of the current stage.\\n\\nThe order of the stages is intentional: each stage builds upon the one before it \u{1F447}\\n\\n```\\nPhase 0 : Setup\\nPhase 1 Auth \u2014 Login\\nPhase 2 Roles & Permissions \u2014 Permissions\\nPhase 3 Inventory \u2014 Stock\\nPhase 4 Sales\\nPhase 5 Purchases\\nPhase 6 Dashboard & Reports\\nPhase 7 Improvements + AI Touches (Optional)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \u{1F7E1} Rules Golden ( stick it on ) (in ` CLAUDE.md` the heart of the project)\\n\\nmarkdown\\nClaude\'s role in this project\\n\\nWe\'re building an ERP system in stages. Follow these rules exactly:\\n\\n## Basic rules\\n1. **Build only one stage at a time.* * Only what is required in the current stage \u2014 do not anticipate future stages .\\n2. **Pause after each stage.* *When you finish, summarize:*\\n- What was done (files + features ).\\n- How do I try it myself (clear steps).\\nAnything that requires a decision from me.\\nThen wait for my approval before you continue.\\n3. **If you need to modify something that already exists, tell me first.** And why \u2014 don\'t change something that\'s working for no reason.\\n4. **Ask if something is unclear** instead of assuming. Wrong assumptions cost us time.\\n\\nCode quality\\n5. Keep the code **simple, clear, and organized** \u2014 expressive names, small files, no repetition.\\n6. Follow the same code pattern as the existing folder . structure (naming , styling ).\\n7. Safety is not a luxury: ** Don\'t put In the code , perform validation on any input , and protect any route according to validation.\\n8. Any modification to the database must be done via ** migration **, not manually.\\n\\n## After each stage\\n9. Create a simple ** seed data ** that I can experiment with.\\n10. Write a **quick test** or at least manual trial steps for the basic flow .\\n11. Suggest a clear ** commit ** message for the stage (stage = commit ).\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \u{1F9F1} The Tech Stack Proposal\\n\\n> A cohesive and AI- friendly stack . If you have a different preference , change it here before you begin.\\n\\n| Class | Technology | Why |\\n|--------|---------|-----|\\n| Framework | **Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript ** | Frontend + API in one place |\\n| Formatting | ** Tailwind CSS + shadcn / ui ** | Fast and clean UI |\\n| Database | ** PostgreSQL ** (or SQLite for a quick start) | Strong relationships |\\n| ORM | **Prisma** | Clear schema + migrations + type- safe |\\n| Login | ** Auth.js ( NextAuth ) ** or ** Lucia ** | Ready and secure |\\n| Validation | ** Zod ** | Checks any input |\\n\\nNote: Start with ** SQLite ** if you want a faster experience without setup , and you can switch to PostgreSQL later.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \u{1F5C2}\uFE0F The Data Model (Complete reference \u2014 we build it table by table with each stage)\\n\\nThis is the final form of the tables. ** We don\'t build it all at once** \u2014 each stage adds its own tables .\\n\\n```\\nUser (id, name , email, password_hash , role_id , is_active , created_at )\\nRole        (id, name, description)                     \u2190 admin / accountant / storekeeper / sales\\nPermission  (id, key, description)                      \u2190 \u0645\u062B\u0627\u0644: \\"sales.create\\", \\"inventory.read\\"\\nRolePermission (role_id, permission_id)\\n\\nCategory    (id, name)\\nProduct     (id, sku, name, category_id, cost_price, sell_price, stock, reorder_level, is_active)\\nStockMovement (id, product_id, type, qty, ref_type, ref_id, note, created_at)  \u2190 in/out/adjust\\n\\nCustomer    (id, name, phone, email, balance)\\nSalesInvoice (id, number, customer_id, user_id, date, status, subtotal, discount, total)\\nSalesItem   (id, invoice_id, product_id, qty, unit_price, line_total)\\n\\nSupplier    (id, name, phone, balance)\\nPurchaseOrder (id, number, supplier_id, user_id, date, status, total)\\nPurchaseItem (id, po_id, product_id, qty, unit_cost, line_total)\\n```\\n\\n**The pivotal relationship:** Any SalesItem decreases Product.stock and performs a StockMovement (out) . Any PurchaseItem increases it and performs a StockMovement (in) . This is the heart of ERP \u2014data moves on its own.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# \u{1F680} Stages\\n\\nEach stage contains: **Goal \xb7 Required \xb7 Not Now \xb7 Finish Mark \xb7 Prompt Ready to Copy**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Setup\\n\\n** Objective: * * A working empty project with a stack + connected database + basic layout + sidebar without any features .\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- Scaffold the project ( Next.js + TS + Tailwind + shadcn / ui ).\\n- Connecting Prisma to the database + First empty migration .\\n- Basic Layout : sidebar containing links to upcoming stages ( placeholders ) + header .\\n- A simple `/` page \\" Hello ERP \\".\\n\\n**Not now :* * Any auth , any real spreadsheet, any feature page .\\n\\n**Completion Mark ( Definition of Done ): **\\n- ` npm run dev ` works without errors.\\n- Prisma is connected and the migration is working.\\n- I check the layout and sidebar in the browser.\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\n> Read CLAUDE.md and ERP-BUILD-GUIDE.md first. We are only in Phase 0 (foundation).\\nCreate a scaffold for the Next.js project (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn / ui ,\\nConnect Prisma to SQLite with the first empty migration , and create a basic layout with a sidebar.\\n> With placeholders for the stages: Auth , Inventory, Sales, Purchases , Dashboard ,\\nA simple homepage. Don\'t build any other features . Let me know when you\'re finished. How do I try? Stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Auth (Login)\\n\\n** Objective: * A user who can log in and out, and the pages are protected.\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- Table ` User` + Auth.js ( credentials : email + password with hashing ).\\n- Page `/ login` , logout , session .\\n- Protecting internal pages (anyone not logged in will be thrown at `/ login` ).\\n- Seed : One admin user to test.\\n\\n**Not now :** Roles and permissions (this is Phase 2 ), i.e., the inventory/sales screen.\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\n- Log in with admin and access the dashboard .\\n- If I\'m not logged in, I can\'t open any internal page.\\n- I logged out successfully.\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe\'re currently in Phase 1 ( Auth ) . Add the User table in Prisma + Auth.js ( credentials ).\\n> email/ password with secure hashing ), page/ login , logout , and protection of all internal pages.\\nCreate a seed account for an admin user to test it. Don\'t do that. roles /permissions Now . Tell me. How\\n> I\'m trying to log in and out, then I\'ll pause for a review.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Roles & Permissions (RBAC)\\n\\n** Objective: * Every user has a role, and every role has permissions, and the system respects them in the UI and API .\\n\\n** Required: **\\nRole` , `Permission`, ` RolePermission` tables + bind ` User.role_id` .\\n- 4 roles: admin / accountant / storekeeper / sales , and permissions in the ` module.action` style .\\n- Helper ` can ( user, \\" sales.create \\") ` is used in the API and UI .\\n- Hide links/buttons based on permissions + reject the API if there are no permissions.\\n- A simple screen for managing users and their roles ( admin only).\\n- Seed : The four users in their respective roles.\\n\\n**Not now :* * Any data module (inventory/sales).\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\n- I\'m in sales and I can\'t see the accounting screens.\\nAPI He refuses any action that is not within my rights, even if I call him by hand .\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe are in Phase 2 ( Roles & Permissions) . Add the Role /Permission/ RolePermission tables.\\n> And link the user to the role. Create 4 roles ( admin, Accountant , storekeeper , sales ) and their permissions\\n> in module.action style , and helper The `can ( )` function applies in both the UI (hide) and API (reject). Work\\nadmin screen for managing users and roles + seed For four users . Don\'t build Modules\\n> Data. Tell me How do I try to differentiate between a turn and a turn, stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Inventory\\n\\n** Objective: * * First real data module \u2014 items, balances and inventory movement.\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- Tables ` Category` , `Product`, ` StockMovement` .\\n- CRUD for items ( list + add + edit ) is protected by the ` inventory .* ` permission.\\n- Display current balance + manual balance adjustment function ` StockMovement` ( adjust ) .\\n- Visual alert if the balance is < ` reorder_level `.\\n- Seed : A few varieties and categories .\\n\\n**Not now :* * Linking inventory to sales/purchases ( will come with each module ).\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\n- I add an item and it appears in the list with its balance.\\n- I manually adjust the balance and the transaction is recorded .\\n- Items that are below the minimum order quantity are distinguished .\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe are in Phase 3 (Inventory) . Add the Category , Product, StockMovement + CRUD tables.\\nFor items protected by inventory privileges , view the balance and enable manual balance adjustment.\\nStockMovement , and highlight items below the order limit. Seed for experimental items. Not tied to sales .\\nNow . Tell me . How do I try? Stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Sales\\n\\n** Objective: * A sales invoice that automatically deducts from inventory \u2014 the most important flow in the system.\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- ` Customer` , ` SalesInvoice` , ` SalesItem` tables .\\n- Sales invoice creation screen (select customer + items + quantities) protected by ` sales .* `.\\n- When saving: Calculate the total + **deduct the quantity from ` Product.stock` ** + perform ` StockMovement` (out) \u2014 all in ** one transaction **.\\n- Sales are prohibited if the balance is insufficient.\\n- Invoice list + Invoice display page.\\n- Customer management ( basic CRUD ).\\n\\n**Not now :** Returns, Advanced Printing, Purchases.\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\n- By creating a sales invoice \u2192 the inventory decreases immediately and the transaction is recorded .\\nI can\'t sell more than the balance.\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe are in Phase 4 (Sales) . Add Customer. SalesInvoice , SalesItem . Create an invoice screen.\\nThe sales (customer + items + quantities) are protected by sales .* When saving, calculate the total and deduct from\\n> Product.stock and perform StockMovement (out) in a single transaction , and prevent the sale if the balance is insufficient.\\nNot enough. Create an invoice list + invoice display + customer CRUD + seed . Don\'t process returns or anything.\\n> Purchases. Tell me How do I try a complete sales cycle, stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Purchases\\n\\n** Objective: * * Purchase order to replenish inventory \u2014 reverse sales.\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- Tables ` Supplier` , ` PurchaseOrder` , ` PurchaseItem` .\\n- Purchase order screen (supplier + items + quantities + cost) protected by ` purchases .* `.\\n- Upon receipt: **increase ` Product.stock` ** + ` StockMovement` (in) in transaction .\\n- Update ` cost_price` for the item (optional) + purchase order list + CRUD for suppliers.\\n\\n**Not now :* * Complex financial calculations, the dashboard .\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\n- By placing a purchase order and receiving it \u2192 the inventory increases and the transaction is recorded.\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe are in Phase 5 ( Purchases ) . Add Supplier. PurchaseOrder , PurchaseItem . Screenshot\\nA purchase order (supplier + items + quantities + cost) is protected by purchases .* , and upon receipt, provide\\n> Product.stock and perform StockMovement (in) in the transaction . Order List + CRUD Suppliers +\\nTell me . How do I try a complete buying cycle? Stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 6 \u2014 Dashboard & Reports\\n\\n** Objective: * * The complete picture \u2014 numbers and graphics collected from all modules .\\n\\n** Required: **\\n- The Dashboard page contains KPIs : Total sales for the month, number of invoices, items under order, top-selling items.\\n- A simple graph (sales in days/months) using a lightweight charts library.\\n- Low stock items report + Top customers report.\\n- Everyone sees according to their own authority.\\n\\n**Not now :* * Advanced PDF/Excel export , AI .\\n\\n**Completion Mark : **\\nAfter I buy/sell, the numbers are in the Dashboard It\'s changing, right?\\n\\n> ** Prompt For copying:* *\\n> ```\\nWe are in Phase 6 (Dashboard) . Create a Dashboard page with KPIs (monthly sales, number\\nInvoices, items below order, best-selling items) + Simple sales graph +\\n> Low-category and high-value customer reports, all within the established guidelines. Tell me. How do I test the numbers?\\n> You speak after a sale/purchase, stop.\\n> ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 7 \u2014 Improvements + AI Touches (Optional)\\n\\n> After the foundation is solid, you can add them one by one (each one being a small phase on its own):\\n\\n- \u{1F916} ** Assistant In Arabic : * * \\" Do it invoice For Ahmed B3 Laptop \u2192 The function is executed (calling ).\\n- \u{1F4C9} ** Expect Stock is depleted ** from the date of sale.\\n- \u{1F4F8} ** Reading Bills Suppliers Image ** ( OCR + AI ).\\n- \u{1F5E3}\uFE0F ** Reports By speaking ** ( Ask In Arabic \u2192 Table / Drawing ).\\n- \u{1F9FE} print Bills PDF , returns, multi- currency , multi- warehouse .\\n\\n> ** Rule:* * Any addition from countries = independent phase , adopts and experiments on its own.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# # \u2705 reminder last\\n\\n- **Stage \u2192 Experience \u2192 Approval \u2192 Next stage .* * There is no \\"Do it all\\".\\n- After each working stage: Make a ** commit ** (this is an excellent time to use Git as we learned ).\\n- If a stage gets too big, divide it in half \u2014 smaller = safer and clearer.\\nIf you feel that the code is still Clinging on , **stop and clean up** before you continue.\\n\\nGood luck \u{1F680} \u2014 Syntax Academy\\n","remark":"  You give one file to Cloud so that he can build a complete ERP system with you **in stages** \u2014 no","owner":"profinformatique76","upvotes":1,"downvotes":0,"upvoteDifference":1,"updatedAt":"2026-07-22T00:32:11.116Z"}')}}]);